      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 381210663,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 1601941479,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777174292711,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Traditional CRSs (pre-LLM) achieve this through hard-coded pipelines and explicit state tracking, \noften relying on slot-filling or finite-state machines. These systems could guide users toward a goal, \nbut their interactions feel rigid and brittle. If a user says something unexpected or nuanced, the system will likely fail to adapt.\n\n\n\nLLM-based systems, by contrast, can improvise, but they often lack structure and consistency in planning, \nmemory, and strategic control. This leads to dialogue that might sound good, but that fails to make progress, loses track of user preferences, or repeats itself.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Traditional CRSs (pre-LLM) achieve this through hard-coded pipelines and explicit state tracking, \noften relying on slot-filling or finite-state machines. These systems could guide users toward a goal, \nbut their interactions feel rigid and brittle. If a user says something unexpected or nuanced, the system will likely fail to adapt.\n\n\n\nLLM-based systems, by contrast, can improvise, but they often lack structure and consistency in planning, \nmemory, and strategic control. This leads to dialogue that might sound good, but that fails to make progress, loses track of user preferences, or repeats itself.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "k8A3X-yxpjcxePv0xpryh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 541.7142857142857,
      "y": 9.857142857142946,
      "width": 565.8995971679688,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
