      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 742196327,
      "version": 71,
      "versionNonce": 261853991,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777174367942,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Multi Agent Conversational Recommender System (MACRS)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multi Agent Conversational Recommender System (MACRS)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DPW64A_SL5f-djJJQENvN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 328.8571428571429,
      "y": 385.5714285714287,
      "width": 1130.359130859375,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2053470345,
      "version": 120,
      "versionNonce": 1971617449,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777174461750,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MACRS merges the strengths of both: strategic planning of traditional systems and the generative fluency of LLMs",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MACRS merges the strengths of both: strategic planning of traditional systems and the generative fluency of LLMs",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "K_K4qG5blY0wfDr0Sljib",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 317.71875,
      "y": 480.7444196428572,
      "width": 1495.638671875,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 59633895,
      "version": 108,
      "versionNonce": 807848135,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777174498947,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This design doesn’t just replicate what traditional CRSs do. It reimagines the architecture using agentic principles: assigning roles, aligning goals, \ncoordinating behavior, and learning from experience. Specifically, MACRS exemplifies a modular agentic architecture that leverages an explicit control loop \nfor dialogue flow, and addresses the inherent coordination costs of multi-agent systems through structured planning and reflection.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This design doesn’t just replicate what traditional CRSs do. It reimagines the architecture using agentic principles: assigning roles, aligning goals, \ncoordinating behavior, and learning from experience. Specifically, MACRS exemplifies a modular agentic architecture that leverages an explicit control loop \nfor dialogue flow, and addresses the inherent coordination costs of multi-agent systems through structured planning and reflection.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "dMp4Xl6TZK1hZJU68OuHt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 321.04464285714283,
      "y": 654.4776785714288,
      "width": 1538.1790771484375,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 138210985,
      "version": 537,
      "versionNonce": 1618447753,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777224917492,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Goals\n- Switch conversation style: ask questions Do you like action movies?, You might enjoy Inception.\n- Learn from behaviour: I don't like horror\n- Decide what to say: One part of the system might want to ask more questions. another might be ready to recommend.\n- Remember what matters: Comedy earlier or searched for romantic movies last week.\n- Keep the conversation on track: The sustem isn't just here to chat. It needs to guide the conversation toward that goal, step-by-step.\n\n\n\n- Multi-agent act planning framework: This module focuses on controlling the dialogue flow by determining the most suitable conversational act at each turn. \nIt involves a collaborative effort between specialized agents to generate and select responses.\n\n- User feedback-aware reflection mechanism: This dynamic optimization module allows MACRS to learn and adapt its behavior based on user interactions, \ncontinually refining its understanding and strategy.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Goals\n- Switch conversation style: ask questions Do you like action movies?, You might enjoy Inception.\n- Learn from behaviour: I don't like horror\n- Decide what to say: One part of the system might want to ask more questions. another might be ready to recommend.\n- Remember what matters: Comedy earlier or searched for romantic movies last week.\n- Keep the conversation on track: The sustem isn't just here to chat. It needs to guide the conversation toward that goal, step-by-step.\n\n\n\n- Multi-agent act planning framework: This module focuses on controlling the dialogue flow by determining the most suitable conversational act at each turn. \nIt involves a collaborative effort between specialized agents to generate and select responses.\n\n- User feedback-aware reflection mechanism: This dynamic optimization module allows MACRS to learn and adapt its behavior based on user interactions, \ncontinually refining its understanding and strategy.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "o6kbI3_cVkGAjulPLp36S",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 543.1381079027354,
